|~ What is declared under `::desc`, the kind of a value turned to
   descend, whose place in the one order is the reverse of its
   payload's: its constructor and the comparisons of values turned. ~|

:desc/construct
  |~~ Lays the kind over any value, its place in the one order turned around. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:desc/gt
  |~~ Answers whether the subject comes after the value the call gives
      among values turned to descend, `1 | desc | gt (2 | desc)`
      answering `true`: under `::desc` the one order runs in reverse, so
      a value comes after another when its payload comes before the
      other's, and the greater payload ranks first, as `sort` and `max`
      rank a key turned by `desc`. A value turned compares with a value
      turned alone: a number given is refused under the value, `1 | desc
      | gt 2`, and is turned first, `gt (2 | desc)`. `gte` answers
      whether the subject comes after the value or ranks with it, `lt`
      and `lte` the reverse.
      ::link~(::desc | doc) ::link~(::any/desc | doc)
      ::link~(::desc/gte | doc) ::link~(::desc/lt | doc)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:desc/gt/answer
  |~~ `true` when the subject comes after the value among values turned
      to descend, `false` otherwise.
  ~~|
  ::boolean

:desc/gt/value
  |~~ The value turned to descend the subject is compared with, computed
      against the subject, `2 | desc | gt (3 | desc)`.
  ~~|
  ~(/0)

:desc/gt/value/NotDescError
  |~~ The value compared is turned to descend, a value of `::desc`. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::desc)

:desc/gt/reversesTheOrder
  |~~ Among values turned to descend, one comes after two. ~~|
  ::law~(1 | desc | gt (2 | desc))

:desc/gt/ranksTheGreaterPayloadFirst
  |~~ The greater payload does not come after the smaller. ~~|
  ::law~(2 | desc | gt (1 | desc) | not)

:desc/gt/value/NotDescError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number given is no value turned to compare with. ~~|
  ::law~(1 | desc | gt 2 !| type | eq ::desc/gt/value/NotDescError)

:desc/gte
  |~~ Answers whether the subject comes after the value the call gives
      among values turned to descend, or ranks with it,
      `2 | desc | gte (2 | desc)` answering `true`. It compares as `gt`
      does, a value turned with a value turned, the smaller payload
      after the greater.
      ::link~(::desc/gt | doc) ::link~(::desc/lte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:desc/gte/answer
  |~~ `true` when the subject comes after the value among values turned
      to descend or ranks with it, `false` otherwise.
  ~~|
  ::boolean

:desc/gte/value
  |~~ The value turned to descend the subject is compared with, computed
      against the subject, `2 | desc | gte (3 | desc)`.
  ~~|
  ~(/0)

:desc/gte/value/NotDescError
  |~~ The value compared is turned to descend, a value of `::desc`. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::desc)

:desc/gte/equalsWithOnePayload
  |~~ Two values turned of one payload rank together. ~~|
  ::law~(2 | desc | gte (2 | desc))

:desc/gte/reversesTheOrder
  |~~ Among values turned to descend, one comes after two. ~~|
  ::law~(1 | desc | gte (2 | desc))

:desc/gte/value/NotDescError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number not turned to descend is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(2 | desc | gte 1 !| type | eq ::desc/gte/value/NotDescError)

:desc/lt
  |~~ Answers whether the subject comes before the value the call gives
      among values turned to descend, `2 | desc | lt (1 | desc)`
      answering `true`: a value comes before another when its payload
      comes after the other's. It compares as `gt` does, a value turned
      with a value turned, and `lte` answers whether the subject comes
      before the value or ranks with it.
      ::link~(::desc/gt | doc) ::link~(::desc/lte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:desc/lt/answer
  |~~ `true` when the subject comes before the value among values turned
      to descend, `false` otherwise.
  ~~|
  ::boolean

:desc/lt/value
  |~~ The value turned to descend the subject is compared with, computed
      against the subject, `2 | desc | lt (3 | desc)`.
  ~~|
  ~(/0)

:desc/lt/value/NotDescError
  |~~ The value compared is turned to descend, a value of `::desc`. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::desc)

:desc/lt/reversesTheOrder
  |~~ Among values turned to descend, two comes before one. ~~|
  ::law~(2 | desc | lt (1 | desc))

:desc/lt/keepsTheSmallerPayloadBehind
  |~~ The smaller payload does not come before the greater. ~~|
  ::law~(1 | desc | lt (2 | desc) | not)

:desc/lt/value/NotDescError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number not turned to descend is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(2 | desc | lt 1 !| type | eq ::desc/lt/value/NotDescError)

:desc/lte
  |~~ Answers whether the subject comes before the value the call gives
      among values turned to descend, or ranks with it,
      `2 | desc | lte (2 | desc)` answering `true`. It compares as `gt`
      does, a value turned with a value turned.
      ::link~(::desc/lt | doc) ::link~(::desc/gte | doc)
  ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:desc/lte/answer
  |~~ `true` when the subject comes before the value among values turned
      to descend or ranks with it, `false` otherwise.
  ~~|
  ::boolean

:desc/lte/value
  |~~ The value turned to descend the subject is compared with, computed
      against the subject, `2 | desc | lte (3 | desc)`.
  ~~|
  ~(/0)

:desc/lte/value/NotDescError
  |~~ The value compared is turned to descend, a value of `::desc`. ~~|
  ::holds~(is ::desc)

:desc/lte/equalsWithOnePayload
  |~~ Two values turned of one payload rank together. ~~|
  ::law~(2 | desc | lte (2 | desc))

:desc/lte/reversesTheOrder
  |~~ Among values turned to descend, two comes before one. ~~|
  ::law~(2 | desc | lte (1 | desc))

:desc/lte/value/NotDescError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number not turned to descend is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(2 | desc | lte 1 !| type | eq ::desc/lte/value/NotDescError)
